The library contains NO third-party code
-----------------------------------------
Everything distributed in this repository was written from scratch for this
project and is covered by its MIT licence:

    ccnbslib.lua     the public entry point
    nbs/*.lua        parsing: reader, header, layers, notes, instruments,
                     decode, analyze, and the CP1252 display converter
    player/*.lua     scheduling: plan, fanout, tempo, dispatch, speaker,
                     clock, runtime
    nbsplay.lua      the minimal command-line player
    tests/**         the local test suite (not published)

There is no `vendor/` directory and nothing here is vendored. Earlier revisions
of this project DID redistribute third-party interface code — a Basalt 2 fork, a
CJK pixel-font renderer, an icon set, and a font fetched at run time. All of it
was deleted when this project became a library, and this file was rewritten
because every claim it used to make had become false. That history is in git.

If a future need arises for a third-party library, that is a decision for the
project owner, not a vendoring detail — and this file must be updated to say
exactly what was taken, from where, and under which licence.


